  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bengal Beverages Pvt. Ltd. & Anr vs Union Of India & Ors on 29 April, 2016 Author: Dipankar Datta Bench: Dipankar Datta 1 29.04.2016 Item No.41 Sb W.P. 7441 (W) of 2016 Bengal Beverages Pvt. Ltd. & Anr. Vs. Union of India & Ors. Mr. S. S. Banerjee, Mr. P. Sancheta, Ms. Payal Saha..........for the petitioners.",
    "facts": "An order passed by the Adjudicating Officer, Kolkata Municipal Corporation under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 dated 08.03.2016 is under challenge in this writ petition. It appears from the impugned order that the adjudicating officer is also the Joint Municipal Commissioner (R&S) of the Corporation. In terms of Section 68 of the Act, an adjudicating officer must be an officer not below the rank of Additional District Magistrate of the District where the alleged offence is committed to be notified by the State Government. Learned advocates appearing for the Corporation are presently not in a position to satisfy this Bench that the incumbent adjudicating officer is equal to the rank of additional district magistrate.",
